WEBVTT

00:01:57.079 --> 00:02:00.621
This consolidation occurs with the help
of a major part of the brain,

00:02:00.663 --> 00:02:03.371
known as “the hippocampus”.

00:02:03.621 --> 00:02:06.163
Its role in long-term memory formation

00:02:06.204 --> 00:02:09.371
was demonstrated in the 1950s
by Brenda Milner

00:02:09.413 --> 00:02:13.954
in her research
with a patient known as H.M.

00:02:14.038 --> 00:02:15.871
After having his hippocampus removed,

00:02:15.913 --> 00:02:20.621
H.M.’s ability to form new 
short-term memories was damaged,

00:02:20.663 --> 00:02:25.288
but he was able to learn 
physical tasks through repetition.

00:02:25.329 --> 00:02:27.371
Due to the removal of his hippocampus,

00:02:27.413 --> 00:02:31.204
H.M.’s ability to form long-term 
memories was also damaged.